/Title (A consecutive-three-absence report belongs in the statistics layer. In a one-script design one file changes; in a module design the utility module and possibly main script change; in a package design stats.py and report.py \(if output is added\) change, with main orchestration updated if necessary.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 488 0 R
>>
endobj
544 0 obj
<<
/Title (import attendance.stats binds the submodule under its package; from attendance import stats imports the submodule name; from attendance.stats import percentage imports the function directly. Packages improve reuse and testing but add a one-time import and small memory cost; modules are cached in sys.modules. All organisations remain O\(n\) for processing n records.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 489 0 R
>>
endobj
545 0 obj
<<
/Title (fest/reader.py reads source files; fest/validation.py validates rows and email; fest/merge.py handles duplicate keys; fest/reports.py writes outputs; main.py orchestrates. For each file, catch file-level OSError; for each line, catch InvalidRecord/ValueError, log and continue; deduplicate with a seen set; write outputs after processing.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 491 0 R
>>
endobj
