/Title (Streaming uses O\(one line\) working memory rather than O\(file size\), closes the file even on exceptions, preserves paise exactly with Decimal, and provides an audit trail of rejected records. Processing time remains O\(n\) for n lines.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 590 0 R
>>
endobj
622 0 obj
<<
/Title (Each CSV line contains register_number,date,status. Use a dictionary keyed by register number with present and total counters. Output one attendance report with percentage and a separate error log with file name, line number, raw content and reason.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 591 0 R
>>
endobj
623 0 obj
<<
/Title (File operations)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 537 0 R
/Prev 591 0 R
/First 629 0 R
/Last 629 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 630 0 R
>>
endobj
624 0 obj
<<
/Title (Trace and complexity)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 537 0 R
/Prev 630 0 R
/First 631 0 R
/Last 631 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 592 0 R
>>
endobj
625 0 obj
<<
/Title (missing field custom InvalidRecord or IndexError if not checked; invalid status/date/number ValueError; empty file)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 538 0 R
/Prev 593 0 R
/Next 594 0 R
>>
endobj
626 0 obj
<<
/Title (InvalidRecord represents a malformed attendance row. parse_line raises it; the file-processing loop catches it, records line number and continues. File-level exceptions are caught by the caller and reported with filename context.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 595 0 R
>>
endobj
627 0 obj
<<
/Title (Complete try structure)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 484 0 R
/Prev 595 0 R
/First 632 0 R
/Last 632 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 596 0 R
>>
endobj
628 0 obj
<<
/Title (Explicit if validation is generally faster and clearer when malformed records are common. Exception-based parsing is concise when bad rows are rare; exceptions have higher overhead when raised repeatedly. Both scan each line once, O\(n\) time.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 596 0 R
>>
endobj
629 0 obj
<<
/Title (Use pathlib.Path.glob to enumerate daily files, mode r with UTF-8 and newline='' for CSV input, and w for freshly generated reports. Iterate line-by-line; use csv.writer for safe output. Append mode is appropriate for a persistent error log across runs.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 623 0 R
>>
endobj
630 0 obj
<<
/Title (Pseudocode)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 537 0 R
/Prev 623 0 R
/First 633 0 R
/Last 633 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 624 0 R
>>
endobj
631 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 624 0 R
>>
endobj
632 0 obj
<<
/Title (Use try for file processing, except for specific expected failures, else for successful completion reporting, and finally for cleanup or completion logging. Use raise FileNotFoundError\(...\) from exc to preserve the original cause. Do not use except Exception: pass because it hides defects such as misspelled variable names.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 627 0 R
>>
endobj
633 0 obj
<<
/Title (BEGIN; initialise attendance map and error list; FOR each daily file: open file; FOR each line with line number: split fields; validate count and P/A status; on invalid append error metadata; otherwise increment total and present; close file; compute each percentage; write below-75% report and error report; END.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 630 0 R
>>
endobj
